CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Permissive

Preamble

CERN has developed this licence to promote collaboration between hardware
designers and to provide a legal tool which supports the freedom to use,
study, modify, share and distribute hardware designs and products based on
those designs. Version 2 of the CERN Open Hardware Licence comes in two
variants: this licence ("CERN-OHL-P") and the reciprocal variant
("CERN-OHL-S").

The CERN-OHL-P is copyright CERN 2020. Anyone is welcome to use it, in
unmodified form only.

Use of this Licence does not imply any endorsement by CERN of any Licensor or
their designs nor does it imply any involvement by CERN in their development.


1 Definitions

  1.1 'Licence' means this CERN Open Hardware Licence.

  1.2 'Compatible Licence' means

       a) any earlier version of the CERN Open Hardware licence;

       b) any version of the CERN-OHL-S or CERN-OHL-P;

       c) any licence which permits You to treat the Source to which it
          applies as licensed under CERN-OHL-S or CERN-OHL-P provided that on
          Conveyance of any such Source, or any associated Product You treat
          the Source in question as being licensed under CERN-OHL-S or
          CERN-OHL-P as appropriate; and

       d) any licence which permits You to treat the Source to which it
          applies as licensed under MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2-Clause,
          BSD-3-Clause, MPL-2.0, LGPL-2.1-or-later, GPL-2.0-or-later, or
          GPL-3.0-or-later.

  1.3 'Source' means information such as design materials or digital code
      which can be applied to Make or test a Product or to prepare a Product
      for use, Conveyance or sale, regardless of its medium or how it is
      expressed. It may include Notices.

  1.4 'Covered Source' means Source that is explicitly made available under
      this Licence.

  1.5 'Product' means any device, component, work or physical object, whether
      in finished or intermediate form, arising from the use, application or
      processing of Covered Source.

  1.6 'Make' means to create or configure something, whether by manufacture,
      assembly, compiling, loading or applying Covered Source or another
      Product or otherwise.

  1.7 'Available Component' means any part, sub-assembly, library or code
      which:

       a) is commercially available or can be made using readily available
          tools and materials; or

       b) is licensed to You under a Compatible Licence.

  1.8 'Convey' means to communicate to the public or distribute.


2 Applicability

  2.1 This Licence governs the use, copying, modification, Conveyance of
      Covered Source and Products, and tells You what rights You have to do
      so.

  2.2 This Licence does not apply to software, firmware, or other code which
      is not part of a Product. Such items are covered by separate licences.

  2.3 If You are an employee or contractor of the Licensor, Your employer's
      or client's internal policies regarding intellectual property do not
      affect Your rights under this Licence.


3 Rights and Obligations

  3.1 Grant of Rights

      Subject to the terms of this Licence, the Licensor grants You a
      perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free licence to:

       a) use, copy, modify, and Convey Covered Source;

       b) Make and Convey Products; and

       c) use Products.

  3.2 Conditions

      The rights granted in Section 3.1 are subject to the following
      conditions:

       a) You must keep intact all Notices in the Covered Source;

       b) When You Convey Covered Source, You must include a copy of this
          Licence;

       c) When You Convey a Product, You must ensure that the recipient has
          access to the Notices required by Section 3.2(a); and

       d) If You modify Covered Source, You must clearly indicate that You
          have done so.

  3.3 No Additional Restrictions

      You may not impose any additional restrictions on the exercise of the
      rights granted under this Licence.


